{
  "area": "items-transactions",
  "description": "Whether a trade may happen, and at what price (US-2 and US-4 of `124-items-equipment-economy`). A transaction is an ACTION in the shared vocabulary rather than a shop mechanism: the resolution carries the atom it is gated as — the world’s own `buyAction` or `sellAction` — and the decision layer asks `permissible/3` about it exactly as it does for an equip, which is what makes a theft a transaction that failed the gate rather than a verb of its own. Each case carries the whole input: the catalogue row, the simulation the price is resolved from, the seller’s supply and whichever purses were actually read. Money fails OPEN when it was never read and CLOSED once it was — the module’s polarity rule applied to coin, because inventing an empty purse would refuse every purchase in a world whose host holds the money. Refusals are evaluated in TRANSACTION_REFUSALS order — unknown, quantity, not_tradeable, out_of_stock, cannot_afford, till_empty — and at least one case is a REFUSED PURCHASE, without which an implementation that sells everything to everybody passes the whole corpus. `forbidden` never appears, for the reason `equipping.json` gives. Regenerate with `npm run items-corpus`.",
